  "blocks": {
    "\"No — progressive disclosure. Reference the style guide as a skill the agent loads when it actually needs to write a component. AGENTS.md pays the token cost every turn.\"": "“不要——使用渐进式披露。把样式指南做成技能，只在智能体真正需要编写组件时加载。AGENTS.md 中的内容每个轮次都要支付 Token 成本。”",
    "\"Should I dump the entire style guide into AGENTS.md?\"": "“应该把整份样式指南都放进 AGENTS.md 吗？”",
    "Loading only the context an agent needs right now, with context pointers to the rest. Borrowed from UI design, where it means showing users only the controls relevant to their current task and hiding the rest behind a click.": "渐进式披露是只加载<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>当前需要的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context\">上下文</a>，其余内容通过<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-pointer\">上下文指针</a>按需获取。这个概念借自 UI 设计，在那里指只向用户展示与当前任务相关的控件，把其余内容隐藏在一次点击之后。",
    "Progressive disclosure inverts this. Keep the always-loaded layer small — a sentence per topic and a pointer to where the detail lives. The agent reads the style guide when it's writing a component, the deployment runbook when it's deploying, and neither when it's fixing a test. Skills are the pattern built into the harness: a short description loaded every session, the full instructions only when triggered.": "渐进式披露把做法反过来：让始终加载的层保持精简——每个主题只留一句说明，再加一个指向详细内容的指针。智能体编写组件时读取样式指南，部署时读取部署手册，修复测试时则两者都不加载。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/skill\">技能</a>就是<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/harness\">运行框架</a>内置的这种模式：简短描述在每次<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>中加载，完整指令只在触发时读取。",
    "The technique exists because context is a cost twice over. Every token loaded up front is billed as input tokens on every turn, and every token spends attention budget whether the agent needs it or not. An AGENTS.md stuffed with the full style guide, deployment runbook, and database conventions makes the agent worse at all of them — the instructions that matter for the current task are diluted by the ones that don't. The tell is an agent that ignores rules you know are in its context: they're in there, but buried.": "这项技术存在，是因为上下文会产生双重成本。预先加载的每个 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/token\">Token</a> 都会在每个<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/turn\">轮次</a>按<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/input-tokens\">输入 Token</a> 计费；无论智能体是否需要，每个 Token 都会消耗<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/attention-budget\">注意力预算</a>。如果 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agents-md\">AGENTS.md</a> 塞满完整样式指南、部署手册和数据库约定，智能体对这几类内容的执行都会变差——当前任务真正需要的指令，会被不相关指令稀释。明显迹象是：智能体忽略了你明知位于上下文中的规则；它们确实在那里，只是被埋住了。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
  },
